  "text": "When your data lives in cloud apps like Notion, Slack, Linear, Figma, or internal company systems, MCP uses a second transport called Streamable HTTP, which replaced the older SSE approach. Instead of running anything locally, your host connects to a normal web address, signs you in securely using OAuth two point one, and streams live updates straight over the web.",
